    { t: "Physiological heat strain", d: "The body's response: rising core temperature, faster heart rate, sweat loss. Two people under the same heat stress can show different strain." },
    { t: "Thermal discomfort", d: "Feeling too hot. It matters for wellbeing and attention, but feeling cooler is not proof of being protected, and feeling fine is not proof of being safe." },
    { t: "Heat-related illness", d: "Harm to health, from heat rash and cramps through heat exhaustion to heat stroke, which is a medical emergency." }
