    { t: "Why the outdoor weather reading may poorly describe a workstation", d: "The city's weather station measures air in open shade away from buildings. A workstation under a hot roof, beside a press or near a loading door has its own conditions. In assessments of Cambodian apparel factories in the hottest months, about half were above the programme's indoor threshold while hotter than the air outside at the same time.", claims: ["c-glw-hotter"] },
    { t: "Why a measure that feels better still needs checking", d: "A fan, a cooling vest or a misting system can feel pleasant at once. Whether it lowers the heat load enough, for the people most exposed, through the whole shift, is a separate question that only measurement and worker feedback answer. Changes also need checking so that they do not add a new risk, such as moving hot air or blocking exhaust ventilation.", claims: [] }
